13. REFERENCES
================================================================

- RFC 2119: Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement
  Levels.
- RFC 8259 / ECMA-404: The JSON Data Interchange Syntax.
- RFC 8785: JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS).
- IEEE 754-2019: IEEE Standard for Floating-Point Arithmetic.
- glTF 2.0 Specification, Khronos Group.


================================================================
14. VERSION HISTORY
================================================================

Version 1.2 (0x03) — incompatible with 1.0, 1.1
  - Removed uvs_present and normals_present booleans; presence
    determined solely by attr_layout (§6.16). Resolves S1.
  - Added normal sign flip for det(M[:3,:3]) < 0 (§8.13).
    Resolves S2.
  - Fixed index-width inequality to n_verts <= 2^(8*W) (§6.12).
    Resolves S3.
  - Pinned canonical float form to RFC 8785 semantics
    (§6.17.4). Resolves S4 without moving world_matrix out of
    JSON.
  - Restated world_matrix bottom-row check in IEEE 754 ==
    terms, accepting -0.0 (§6.6, §7.11). Resolves S5.
  - Restated normal unit-length check as magnitude error, not
    per-component (§7.25). Resolves S6.
  - Dropped duplicate-descriptor validation rule entirely;
    instancing is a legitimate case (§8.24). Resolves S7.
  - Added 4-byte alignment for attribute blocks (§5.6, §8.22).
    Resolves S8.
  - Restated §12 to attribute resource bounds to §7.30–§7.32,
    not §7.21. Resolves S9.
  - Clarified JSON integer range and derived offset bounds
    (§6, §6.7, §6.8, §6.10, §6.11, §6.13). Resolves S10.
  - Made material_name nullable; removed "none" reservation
    (§6.5, §7.27, §7.28). Resolves S11.
  - Tightened §8.26 to specify determinism per writer version
    and clarify extension-field responsibility. Resolves S12.
  - Required attr_layout sorting by name (§6.15), fixing
    canonicalization coverage. Resolves S13.
  - Added §10.3 stating instanced primitives are duplicated;
    no cross-descriptor sharing. Resolves S14.
  - Lowered §7.2 minimum file length to 10. Resolves S15.
  - Stated explicitly that this spec defines TMB 1.2 with
    magic 0x03 (§2, §5.1). Resolves S16.
  - §8.15 now specifies that absent mode defaults to
    TRIANGLES. Resolves nit on §8.14.
  - §11 specifies round-half-to-even for the JSON variant's
    4-decimal rounding. Resolves nit on §11.
  - §6.15 constrains extension name characters to [a-z0-9_]+.
    Resolves nit on §6.17.
  - §6.6 restates row-major in the body, not only in §14.
    Resolves nit on §6.6.
  - Changed magic fourth byte from 0x02 to 0x03.

Version 1.1 (0x02) — superseded
  - Moved UVs and normals to attribute blob.
  - Added adaptive index width.
  - Added world-space normals contract (without sign flip).
  - Added round-trip determinism (JSON canonicalization as
    first specified).
  - Multiple correctness fixes vs. 1.0.

Version 1.0 (0x01) — superseded
  - Initial draft.